# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase core, story MOCK3-1.

LOCATED FIX SITE(S) — traced in this repository before you were asked. Anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces:
- src/fares.ts :: fareFor — fareFor() computes the fare amount for each rider. Line 10 uses a strict > comparison for the age 65 threshold instead of >=, causing riders aged exactly 65 to skip the senior concession check and receive the base fare (350 cents) instead of the concession fare (175 cents). The function comment (line 7) explicitly states the rule is '65 AND OVER', but the code implements only '> 65'.


DECLARED FILES — the actual contents of the files this story names or the detective located. Base every observable criterion on what THIS code does, not on what the title suggests:
--- src/fares.ts
/** Fare rules for a transit line. Ages are whole years. */
export type Rider = { age: number; hasPass: boolean };

export const BASE_FARE_CENTS = 350;
export const CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS = 175;

/** Riders aged 65 AND OVER pay the concession fare. */
export function fareFor(rider: Rider): number {
  if (rider.hasPass) return 0;
  if (rider.age > 65) return CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS;
  if (rider.age < 13) return CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS;
  return BASE_FARE_CENTS;
}

export function totalFor(riders: Rider[]): number {
  return riders.reduce((sum, r) => sum + fareFor(r), 0);
}



